n class=\"codebook-toc-label\">Laws of UX</span><span class=\"v2-nav-provenance\">Jon Yablonski</span></span><span class=\"v2-nav-pending\">5</span><span class=\"sw mini \" role=\"switch\" tabindex=\"0\" aria-checked=\"true\" aria-label=\"Laws of UX\"></span></a><button type=\"button\" class=\"bn-btn bn-btn-secondary bn-btn-sm\" data-testid=\"bn-v2-nav-browse\">Browse Codebooks</button></nav></div><div class=\"drag-handle toc-drag-handle\" role=\"separator\" aria-orientation=\"vertical\" aria-valuenow=\"240\" aria-valuemin=\"200\" aria-valuemax=\"480\" aria-label=\"Resize table of contents\" tabindex=\"0\"></div></div>", "section": "<section data-testid=\"bn-codebook-v2\"><div class=\"section-heading\"><h1>Codebook</h1><div class=\"section-heading-action\"><button class=\"bn-btn bn-btn-secondary bn-btn-lg\" data-testid=\"bn-v2-browse\">Browse Codebooks</button></div></div><div class=\"v2-layout\"><div class=\"v2-main\"><div data-testid=\"bn-v2-page\"><div class=\"pg-head\"><div class=\"pg-headmain\"><div class=\"pg-titlerow\"><div class=\"pg-titletext\"><div class=\"pg-title\">Bristlenose UXR Codebook</div><div class=\"pg-author prov-system\">Available by default</div></div><div class=\"pg-titleaction\"><button class=\"bn-btn bn-btn-secondary framework-remove-btn\" data-testid=\"bn-v2-uninstall\">Uninstall</button></div></div><div class=\"pg-review-row\"><span class=\"pg-review-meta\">34 tags · applied to 10 quotes in Demo study<span class=\"undec\"> · 9 tentative</span></span><button class=\"bn-btn bn-btn-secondary bn-btn-sm\" data-testid=\"bn-v2-review\">Review</button></div><div class=\"pg-desc bn-lead-para\"><p class=\"bn-lead-claim\"><strong>A practitioner-oriented codebook for any user research study.</strong></p><p class=\"bn-lead-rest\">Eight theme groups covering behaviour, pain points, needs, mental models, motivation, emotion, context, and learning. Domain-agnostic — works equally well for fishkeeping, fintech, healthcare, or rock climbing. These are universal patterns of human experience that emerge in qualitative research across any domain.</p></div></div><div class=\"pg-side\"><div class=\"preview-author\" data-testid=\"bn-v2-author\"><div class=\"preview-author-bio\">This is the default codebook — it provides a general-purpose qualitative coding framework that applies to any domain. Unlike the Research Leaders codebooks (Garrett, Norman), which focus on designed artefacts and specific interaction-design theories, these tags reflect the practical vocabulary used by working UX researchers on sticky notes, in Dovetail, and in affinity diagrams.</div></div></div></div><div class=\"v2-groups\" style=\"--bn-count-digits: 1;\"><div class=\"codebook-group\" style=\"background-color: var(--bn-group-ux);\"><div class=\"group-header\"><div class=\"group-title-area\"><div class=\"group-title\"><span class=\"group-title-text\">Behaviour</span></div><p class=\"group-subtitle\">What people actually do</p></div></div><div class=\"tag-list\"><div id=\"code-8\" class=\"tag-row\"><div class=\"tag-name-area\"><span class=\"badge\" style=\"background-color: var(--bn-ux-1-bg);\">workaround</span></div><span class=\"tag-bar-area\"><span class=\"tag-bar-track\"></span><span class=\"tag-count\">0</span></span></div><div id=\"code-9\" class=\"tag-row\"><div class=\"tag-name-area\"><span class=\"badge\" style=\"background-color: var(--bn-ux-2-bg);\">habit</span></div><span class=\"tag-bar-area\"><span class=\"tag-bar-track\"></span><span class=\"tag-count\">0</span></span></div><div id=\"code-10\" class=\"tag-row\"><div class=\"tag-name-area\"><span class=\"badge\" style=\"background-color: var(--bn-ux-3-bg);\">avoidance</span></div><span class=\"tag-bar-area\"><span class=\"tag-bar-track\"></span><span class=\"tag-count\">0</span></span></div><div id=\"code-11\" class=\"tag-row\"><div class=\"tag-name-area\"><span class=\"badge\" style=\"background-color: var(--bn-ux-4-bg);\">say-do gap</span></div><span class=\"tag-bar-area\"><span clas